#!/bin/sh
# Pre-commit is `next` itself, offline and fast: generation, typecheck, tests, Lean, audit, purify. Whatever honesty it finds is
# already in the leads docket when the commit lands; it never blocks. The generated files it rewrote join the commit.
npm run next -- --offline --fast
git add -u -- docs/public/mcp.json docs/mcp.md docs/.vitepress/config.mts src/quantum/clay-statements.ts README.md 2>/dev/null
exit 0
